course: dictionary
lesson: 5787
title: Lyrical
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Lyrical describes writing or music that is beautiful and smooth, like a song or a poem. A lyrical piece uses lovely words and shows strong feelings. The words around it give you clues to its meaning.
explain: In the Mole's story, he «talked casually» about the harvest, which sounds ordinary. Then he «became simply lyrical», so he began to speak like a poem. The change tells you that lyrical means full of song-like beauty.
explain: Be careful: lyrics are the words of a song, but lyrical is a describing word. A lyrical tune is smooth and singing. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: "he became simply song-like" still makes sense.
explain: You can also wax lyrical about something. This means you talk about it happily and for a long time, with great enthusiasm. Grandma might wax lyrical about her garden, going on and on because she loves it.
fact: Lyrical means beautiful and full of feeling, like a song or a poem.
fact: «Lyrical» can also describe music that is smooth and singing.
fact: «Lyrics» means the words of a song, and it is a different word from lyrical.
fact: «Wax lyrical» means to talk about something with great enthusiasm.
fact: In «and then he became simply lyrical», the Mole speaks like a poem.
exercise: In «and then he became simply lyrical», what does lyrical mean? | Spoke in a loud, angry voice | Fell asleep while talking | Wrote a long list of rules | *Spoke like a poem, full of beauty
exercise: Which word means the words of a song? | Lyrical | *Lyrics | Lyre, an old harp-like instrument
exercise: Grandma says she will wax lyrical about her holiday. What does this mean? | Sing it very badly | *Talk about it happily and for a long time | Forget all about it | Write it down in a list
test: Which meaning best fits a lyrical tune? | Broken and short | *Smooth and singing | Loud and bouncing | Quiet and sad
test: Mia reads «a lyrical description of the sea». What does lyrical praise? | Writing that is very short | Dull, plain writing | Writing with lots of numbers | *Writing that sounds musical and full of feeling
exam: Which sentence best shows what lyrical means in the Mole's story? | *He began speaking like a poem, full of beauty | He began to eat his lunch | He began speaking very quietly | He stopped talking altogether
